### Version

v27.0.0-v8-canary2026101812b4708d0e (V8 15.8.21). Not reproducible on v26.12.0 (V8 14.6.202.34).

### Platform

```text
Darwin 24.6.0 arm64 (macOS)
```

### Subsystem

node-api (root cause in V8 heap)

### What steps will reproduce the bug?

This is a Node-API addon that wraps 1 MiB of native memory per object, reports it with `napi_adjust_external_memory`, and releases it in a normal (non-basic) `napi_wrap` finalizer. The script drops every object immediately and yields to the event loop every 100 allocations.

`addon.c`:

```c
#include <node_api.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

#define SIZE (1 << 20)
static int64_t live = 0;

static void finalize(napi_env env, void* data, void* hint) {
  int64_t ignored;
  free(data);
  live--;
  napi_adjust_external_memory(env, -SIZE, &ignored);
}

static napi_value Make(napi_env env, napi_callback_info info) {
  napi_value obj;
  int64_t ignored;
  void* mem = malloc(SIZE);
  live++;
  napi_create_object(env, &obj);
  napi_adjust_external_memory(env, SIZE, &ignored);
  napi_wrap(env, obj, mem, finalize, NULL, NULL);
  return obj;
}

static napi_value Live(napi_env env, napi_callback_info info) {
  napi_value result;
  napi_create_int64(env, live, &result);
  return result;
}

static napi_value Init(napi_env env, napi_value exports) {
  napi_value fn;
  napi_create_function(env, "make", NAPI_AUTO_LENGTH, Make, NULL, &fn);
  napi_set_named_property(env, exports, "make", fn);
  napi_create_function(env, "live", NAPI_AUTO_LENGTH, Live, NULL, &fn);
  napi_set_named_property(env, exports, "live", fn);
  return exports;
}

NAPI_MODULE(NODE_GYP_MODULE_NAME, Init)
```

`binding.gyp`:

```json
{ "targets": [ { "target_name": "addon", "sources": ["addon.c"] } ] }
```

`run.js`:

```js
const { make, live } = require("./build/Release/addon.node");
(async () => {
  let peak = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < 20000; i++) {
    make();
    if (i % 100 === 99) {
      peak = Math.max(peak, live());
      await new Promise((r) => setImmediate(r));
    }
  }
  console.log(`${process.version} (V8 ${process.versions.v8}): peak live = ${peak} MiB`);
})();
```

```sh
npx node-gyp rebuild --nodedir=/path/to/node
node run.js
```

### How often does it reproduce? Is there a required condition?

Always on the v8-canary build. The condition is that native memory reported with `napi_adjust_external_memory` is released from a normal finalizer, i.e. after the GC that found the object dead.

### What is the expected behavior? Why is that the expected behavior?

The amount of dead native memory waiting for collection should stay bounded, as it does on v26.12.0:

```text
v26.12.0 (V8 14.6.202.34-node.39): peak live = 136 MiB
```

### What do you see instead?

```text
v27.0.0-v8-canary2026101812b4708d0e (V8 15.8.21-node.7): peak live = 5660 MiB
```

GCs back off geometrically. `--trace-gc --trace-gc-verbose --trace-gc-nvp` shows the global allocation limit tracking the garbage, at 64, 117, 204, 272, 461, … MB.

Using a basic finalizer (`NAPI_EXPERIMENTAL`, which Node calls from the first-pass weak callback) keeps the peak at about 1 MB.

### Additional information

The root cause is in V8, filed as https://issues.chromium.org/issues/574627777, which includes a stock-V8-API repro.

Since V8 14.8 (6a5039d9db9, `external_memory_accounted_in_global_limit` on by default), V8 computes the global allocation limit inside the GC pause from external memory that still includes the objects that GC just found dead. Memory released after the pause never lowers that limit. That covers second-pass callbacks and the normal Node-API finalizers queued by `napi_env__::InvokeFinalizerFromGC`.

Normal finalizers are the Node-API default, so native addons that hold large buffers will be affected once Node ships a V8 with this scheme. On v26 the same behavior can be previewed with `--external-memory-accounted-in-global-limit`. 14.6's implementation of that flag differs, though, so the canary is the faithful repro.

The scheme is also discussed in #61967 as the expected fix for the Buffer regression there.

